cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Ca-Sr-O thermodynamic database for Thermo-Calc"
message: "If you use this database, please cite it as indicated here, and cite the original assessments listed in the README as well."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "Cruz-Cervantes"
    given-names: "Fernando Ivan"
    affiliation: "Instituto Politécnico Nacional"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-6155-918X"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-13"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  CALPHAD description of the Ca-Sr-O system for Thermo-Calc, with the liquid
  phase in the associate model (Ca, CaO, O, Sr, SrO). It assembles five
  published descriptions that used mutually incompatible models: the
  two-sublattice Sr-O ionic liquid is converted analytically to associates, the
  two-state CaO liquid is refitted to classical SGTE form imposing the melting
  point and the enthalpy of fusion, and the halite (Ca,Sr)O solid solution is
  validated by two independent routes. The stoichiometric phases CaO and CaO2
  keep the third generation Einstein functions. It includes the Console Mode
  macros, the PARROT POP file and the experimental data used.
keywords:
  - CALPHAD
  - thermodynamic database
  - Thermo-Calc
  - Ca-Sr-O
  - calcium oxide
  - strontium oxide
  - associate solution model
  - phase diagram
